<UnionCaseLayout title="Union Klinika — Google Ads" description="Google Search acquisition architecture for Union Klinika in Riga." eyebrow="GOOGLE ADS" headline="Be there when" accent="patients search." intro="For a medical clinic, search is the channel closest to existing intent. We built the Google Ads layer around bilingual demand, clinic services and a website designed to receive that traffic." metrics={[{value:'GOOGLE',label:'high-intent channel'},{value:'RU / LV',label:'bilingual structure'},{value:'SEARCH',label:'intent-led campaigns'},{value:'CLINIC',label:'appointment destination'}]}>
<section class="case-section shell"><div class="two"><span class="eyebrow">THE ROLE OF SEARCH</span><div><h2>Meta creates demand.<br/>Google catches it.</h2><p class="statement">A person searching for a consultation or clinic service is already much closer to action than a passive audience.</p><p>The project included a dedicated Google Ads workstream and bilingual ad architecture. We connect the search message to the relevant service destination instead of sending every click to a generic homepage.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="case-section dark"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">REPRESENTATIVE JOURNEY</span><div class="flow"><span>PATIENT NEED</span><b>→</b><span>GOOGLE SEARCH</span><b>→</b><span>RU / LV AD</span><b>→</b><span>RELEVANT SERVICE PAGE</span><b>→</b><span>APPOINTMENT ACTION</span></div><p class="note">The project KPI sheet does not contain verified Google conversion totals for the period shown, so we deliberately do not publish a conversion or CPA figure here.</p></div></section>
<section class="accent-section"><div class="shell"><span class="eyebrow">PRINCIPLE</span><h2>Capture intent.<br/>Do not invent demand.</h2></div></section>
